==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
This Zombie Outbreak stage is essentially just the original with some Zigges added. Given their ability to burrow and the low Cat Deploy Limit, they can be somewhat problematic, especially since multiple Elizabeth the LVIths spawn in to cause problems with waves.

[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] is still effective, though units such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cat]] and [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]] are still recommended for the Zigges. Additionally, [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] are good options for the Elizabeths here, as they are still the main threat of this stage.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
The Zombie Outbreak on this stage retains aspects from Chapter 1 but now with a different cast of enemies. For example: the addition of Formicidaean Ariant. It also switches Zigge for Cadaver Bear, which adds another challenge due to the distinct lack of dedicated non-Uber counters.

Despite its difficult choice of enemies, like any stage, there are ways to work around things here. If you have access to them, [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] are fantastic counters to burrowing Formicidaean Ariants, given their Z-Kill and high-DPH. The Cadaver Bears are spaced out in such a way that you can you can chip them down with the likes of [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs & Fenrir]] and/or [[Talents|Talented]] [[Archer Cat (Rare Cat)|Cataur]], before Holy Blasting them to ensure the kill goes through. Make Sure to include Wave Blockers like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] or [[Gloomy Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Witchy Neneko]] so that your units don't get sniped by Elizabeth's Wave Attacks.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This Zombie Outbreak stage is similar to Chapter 1 but now with hard-pushing melee units like Bore and Dread Bore. This stage may look daunting, but it is actually even easier than the previous chapter with a simple rush strategy. Simply burst down Bore with Courier Cat and iCat, then gun down the base with [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]].

If you find yourself unable to rush, you can also abuse the two Bores' high DPS to constantly kill your meat shields, rendering Elizabeth unable to snipe your cats with Wave Attacks. This way you can kill the Bore and Dread Bore in a more conventional way that is less risky.

